---
/*
  The six fears in the order they came up in our own calls.
  04-konzept.md section 4.3, page "/faq", derived from 03, section 4.
  Every answer links into the mechanism it rests on. No absolute safety
  promise anywhere on this page, appendix A of the closing playbook blocks it.

  DECIDED (Manuel, 07.09.2026): the contract answer names no term or notice
  period, only that terms are discussed on the call and early exit stays open.
  Der Split steht nicht auf der Seite, "on the agreed split" bleibt ohne Zahl.

  Sprache: einfaches Englisch, Ansage Manuel 07.09.2026 abends. Diese Strings
  werden als Text gerendert und deshalb von der Lesbarkeitspruefung
  mitgemessen, siehe scripts/check-copy.mjs, Regel 5.
*/
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CtaBlock from '../components/CtaBlock.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What if my account gets banned?',
    a: [
      'We work through official tools. We keep the messages our system sends inside a hard limit. We do not use the growth tricks that get accounts flagged. That lowers the risk. It does not take the risk away. No agency can take it away.',
      'If it happens, the fix is the work. We appeal where an appeal exists. We build the reach back on the accounts you still have. We move the fans you already earned. You do not start from nothing.',
    ],
    link: { href: '/how-it-works#access', label: 'How access works' },
  },
  {
    q: 'Who can get into my accounts?',
    a: [
      'You do not hand us a password. We post to Instagram through Zernio. We run the OnlyFans chat and vault through Infloww. Both are official tools, and you can take their access back.',
      'Our team signs in to our own systems with company accounts. We use no shared logins. Your portal login is kept apart from the staff system. It can never hold a staff role.',
      'Two step login for your own accounts is the next question. So is what changes when someone leaves our team. We have no written answer for either one yet. Ask us on the call and we will tell you where it stands today.',
    ],
    link: { href: '/how-it-works#access', label: 'How access works' },
  },
  {
    q: 'Who writes to my fans, and what do they say?',
    a: [
      'A trained chat team. They work from what you set at the start. Your limits. Your prices. Your no go list.',
      'Twice a week our system scores the last finished shift. It uses a written score sheet and a fixed pass mark. Some mistakes fail on the spot. We also measure how fast the reply came. The person who wrote is never the person who scores.',
      'So a colleague reads the work, on a fixed plan, against a written sheet. We write down who writes in your name. You may tell your fans that. We will not ask you to take the line out of your bio.',
    ],
    link: { href: '/how-it-works#chatting', label: 'How the check works' },
  },
  {
    q: 'How long is the deal, and how do I get out?',
    a: [
      'We go through the terms on the call. You can leave early if this stops working for you.',
    ],
    link: { href: '/switching', label: 'If you are switching from another agency' },
  },
  {
    q: 'What about leaks?',
    a: [
      'It is the internet. Nobody gets content fully off it again. No one can promise you that.',
      'Here is what can be done. We send takedown notices where the site takes them. We watermark. We keep your best paid material off the channels that get copied first. We tell you which of those we do for you, and which ones need you.',
    ],
    link: null,
  },
  {
    q: 'How and when do I get paid?',
    a: [
      'OnlyFans pays your own bank first. We send our bill after that, once a week, on the agreed split. Your money does not run through us on the way to you.',
      'We do not give tax or bank advice. When your case needs it, ask your accountant. We would rather say that than guess.',
    ],
    link: null,
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="FAQ | Wunder"
  description="The six questions creators really ask us, with the answer and the reason behind it."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap wrap-narrow">
      <h1>The six questions we really get.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        In the order they come up. Every answer says what we do, not what we promise.
      </p>
      <div class="faq-list">
        {
          faqs.map((item) => (
            <article class="faq-item">
              <h2>{item.q}</h2>
              {item.a.map((paragraph) => (
                <p>{paragraph}</p>
              ))}
              {item.link && (
                <p class="caption">
                  <a href={item.link.href}>{item.link.label}</a>
                </p>
              )}
            </article>
          ))
        }
      </div>
      <CtaBlock />
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .faq-list {
    margin-top: 40px;
  }

  .faq-item {
    padding: 32px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .faq-item h2 {
    font-size: 22px;
    text-transform: none;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.012em;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .faq-item p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
</style>
